"shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"6cHHsYrRlkVTZxWyLQm9hQ","review_id":"C6eUMBJKfkcfEr2LjKcMdw","date":"2017-10-15T21:32:09","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9300622344017029,"text_excerpt":"So happy they take credit cards now. They probably don't need any reviews but they have really good hot sausage. I am not a hot sausage eater but felt like one on a Saturday afternoon. Took my girls down there and ate across the street at a outside eatery. The cook in there has been working there forever. They have a great menu selection of different po boys and sandwiches as well."},{"business_id":"6cHHsYrRlkVTZxWyLQm9hQ","review_id":"aau-x-lVdzqFk_CLYaV-7w","date":"2014-05-20T23:47:14","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9242314100265503,"text_excerpt":"I'm not gonna lie. The first time I went to this place, it looked like sketch ville USA. I was a little weary of this little Magazine St. market, but my friend told me that the food is really good, so I decided to give it the benefit of the doubt. They have a lot of \"take out\" type of food and I decided that the hot sausage po boy was as good as anything to try. For just under $10, it was a real deal for the size. After I got it home, I was blown away at how good it was! It was packed with sausage and had a lot of flavor. It ALMOST tasted as if I had ordered it from a real po boy place. I highly recommend this weird little convenience store that makes good sandwiches."},{"business_id":"6cHHsYrRlkVTZxWyLQm9hQ","review_id":"IW1W8sw5acA0l-qk6nvfpw","date":"2011-04-11T20:27:29","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.901879072189331,"text_excerpt":"I LOVE THEIR po-boys, chicken, fried rice! They have candy, sodas, beer, chips, and all that good stuff. Good through mardi gras! Convenient since it's on magazine street so you can just walk down to magazine street before the parade starts to grab some hot food since it's cold outside!"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"6cHHsYrRlkVTZxWyLQm9hQ","photo_id":"DLtonayt-IDE5s5kqPH0BA","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/DLtonayt-IDE5s5kqPH0BA.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0000001192092896}]},"notebook_case":null}
